# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify `_redirects` file format.
# Wave 2026-07-grand-uplift / W5 (deploy Option A).
#
# NOTE on /api/*: this file intentionally does NOT declare an `/api/*`
# rewrite/proxy rule to an external API origin. Cloudflare Pages' 200-status
# rewrites only ever serve local static assets from this project — unlike
# Netlify, CF Pages does NOT proxy a 200-rewrite through to an external
# origin. A rule like `/api/*  https://some-api-host/:splat  200` here would
# silently no-op (or 404) on Cloudflare Pages, not actually proxy.
#
# The FastAPI reference API this app talks to (relative `/api/v1/...` fetches
# in src/games/sudoku/composables/useApi.ts, resolved same-origin via
# `document.baseURI`) is wired one of two ways, both owner-side and outside
# this repo's static config:
#   1. Build-time: `VITE_API_URL` set to the API origin so the built bundle
#      calls it directly (cross-origin from the browser's perspective; the
#      `_headers` CSP's `connect-src` would then need that origin added).
#   2. Edge-time: a Cloudflare Worker route in front of this Pages project
#      that proxies `/api/*` to the API origin, keeping calls same-origin
#      from the browser (no CSP change needed).
# The API origin's hostname is unknown as of this wave (OD-5, owner action,
# AWS App Runner box being stood up) — do not fabricate or hardcode it here.
#
# SPA fallback: everything else resolves client-side (no router yet, but the
# app is a single entry point regardless — this just guards against a direct
# hit on any path other than `/` 404ing instead of loading the app shell).
/*    /index.html    200
